# Rust build artifacts.
#
# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — it should be committed once it
# can be generated (blocked today: the ../tamga-rust path dependency in
# Cargo.toml doesn't resolve to a real crate yet, so `cargo generate-lockfile`
# fails). This is a binary-artifact-producing crate (cdylib/staticlib), not a
# library meant to be consumed by other Cargo projects, so an intentionally
# committed lockfile is the right call here, not optional noise.
/target/

# CMake build directories (corrosion + the tests/c/ CTest harness +
# examples/). Multiple possible locations depending on how a consumer
# configures out-of-tree builds. build-asan/ is CLAUDE.md's documented
# AddressSanitizer build tree (`cmake -S . -B build-asan -DTAMGA_C_ENABLE_ASAN=ON`).
/build/
/build-asan/
tests/c/build/
examples/build/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# CMake build trees
build/
build-*/

# Test key material is generated, never committed -- see
# tests/fixtures/keys/generate.sh
*.pem

# The fixture generator is a dev-only tool; its build output is not tracked.
tools/fixture-generator/target/
tools/fixture-generator/Cargo.lock

# Local install trees produced by `cmake --install --prefix`
staging/
